# No left-border accents

Never mark something as special with a colored or thick border on its left
(or inline-start) edge. This applies to callouts, quotes, cards, table rows
and cells, alerts, active nav items, list items, and form sections.

Also avoid look-alikes: an inset left box-shadow, a `::before` bar pinned to
the left edge, or a `border-inline-start`.

```css
/* ❌ BAD */
.topRow th { border-left: 5px solid var(--cta); }
.callout { border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); padding-left: 1rem; }

/* ✅ GOOD: use tint, a full outline, a badge, or an icon */
.topRow { background: var(--top-row); }
.callout { background: var(--tint); border-radius: 1rem; }
```

A neutral 1px divider that separates two columns of a grid (it's on the left
edge only because of layout, and it's the same color as other dividers) is a
divider, not an accent, and is allowed.
